# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-adapters-cmake: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
#### module CMake checkout integration adapter

Detect a consumer root `CMakeLists.txt`. The lifecycle composes this build adapter with the single
submodule materialization and passes `Export.Path` as the consumer-root-relative source directory.
This adapter never clones, copies, updates, or removes that checkout.

#### decision One generated include and one owned root line

Write dependency blocks to `deps/git-a2a.cmake`, sorted by dependency name. Each block calls
`add_subdirectory` for `Export.Path`. The root file gets exactly
`include("deps/git-a2a.cmake") # git-a2a`; remove only that marked line and only when the generated
file has no dependency blocks. Never edit other CMake content.

#### invariant Pull resolves an existing checkout without building the application

Capability is read-only and returns a typed not-wirable reason for an empty, `.`, absolute, or
escaping checkout path. Pull requires the submodule-owned source directory, writes the integration,
and runs CMake configure into `.git-a2a/build/cmake`; it does not compile the whole consumer.
Remove deletes only owned integration and reconfigures when other managed CMake dependencies
remain. Removing the last one deletes the adapter-owned configure tree, because configuring a
consumer that still references the intentionally removed target would make removal impossible.
Inspect reports both declaration drift and a missing checkout.

#### test Golden lifecycle

Tests cover private editor idempotence, Inspect, read-only Capability, clean and changed
declarations, byte-restoring removal, sorted blocks, missing
checkouts, and safe repair/removal of foreign bytes in the wholly owned generated file.

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

